# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local secrets / credentials (never commit)
.env

# Cloudflare's local cache
.wrangler/

# Scratch / temp files
*.tmp
*.part

# Local backup of the old precompiled UI (kept on disk, not deployed)
_legacy_index.html
_schema_probe.json

# Photos move to Cloudflare R2 on their own once the R2_* secrets are set: pull.py
# copies each one, checks the public URL, and removes the repo copy on later runs.
# Add "photos/" here after that finishes.

# Private data: the photo list, photo history, camera spots, tags, notes, comments
# and uploads live in the private R2 bucket under state/ (state_sync.py and the
# Worker). Never commit them: GitHub Pages would serve them to anyone.
data.js
.prev-data.js
.state-hashes
store.json
tags.json
ai-tags.json
comments.json
uploads.json
cameras.json
camera-names.json
metadata.json
weather.json
forecast.json
